# AI Gateway configuration
# Provide keys for the models you intend to use.
GEMINI_API_KEY="your_gemini_api_key_here"
OPENAI_API_KEY="your_openai_api_key_here"

# Access token every client must send as "Authorization: Bearer <token>".
# Without it the gateway refuses all requests rather than running open. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
# then paste the same value into the Android app under Settings > AI gateway.
AURORA_GATEWAY_TOKEN=""

# --- Signing in with Google, instead of sharing a token -----------------------
#
# Both are required together. A client ID with no allowlist would accept an ID
# token from every Google account there is, which for a gateway holding provider
# keys means handing the bill to the internet. With either missing, ID-token
# authentication is off and AURORA_GATEWAY_TOKEN is the only way in.
#
# The client ID is the same one the Android app was built with - the token has to
# have been issued for this application, and that is what is checked.
AURORA_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""

# Comma-separated. Either the Google account's email address or its subject id.
# An email only counts when Google reports it as verified; a subject id always
# counts, because it is Google's own and cannot be claimed.
AURORA_ALLOWED_ACCOUNTS=""
